{"chunk_id": "9c1f75a12cc4", "text": "On Mount Rishyamuka, the exiled monkey king Sugriva spots the armed princes Rama and Lakshmana approaching the forest. Terrified that his powerful brother Bali has sent assassins, Sugriva panics and flees from peak to peak with his monkey companions. His minister Hanuman calms him, arguing that Bali is nowhere nearby and urging clear judgment instead of fear. Sugriva, still wary of royal intrigue, decides caution is wiser than flight. He orders Hanuman to approach the strangers in disguise as a common man, observe their speech, gestures, and intentions, and win their trust through courtesy and praise. Thus begins the pivotal encounter that will unite Rama and the vanara kingdom\u2014Hanuman\u2019s first meeting with Rama, a moment that will spark the alliance leading to the search for Sita and the coming war with Ravana.\nSugriva, fearing Bali\u2019s plot, sends Hanuman in disguise to investigate the identities and intentions of the armed strangers Rama and Lakshmana.\nThemes: fear of Bali, caution and espionage, Hanuman\u2019s diplomacy, first approach to Rama, leadership under fear", "vector": [0.001970752142369747, -0.03552377223968506, -0.004895904567092657, -0.0034224449191242456, 0.0018083368195220828, 0.02474072575569153, -0.01002622302621603, -0.012176134623587132, -0.018900468945503235, -0.020360533148050308, 0.00029343614005483687, -0.005930675193667412, -0.000655103474855423, 0.0034257937222719193, 0.004132384434342384, -0.0005378964706324041, 0.05100849270820618, -0.01985151879489422, 0.007481156382709742, -0.019195159897208214, 0.0060512307099998, -0.0033102610614150763, -0.012832493521273136, -0.012417245656251907, -0.024888072162866592, 0.007876311428844929, 0.026870544999837875, -0.029254870489239693, 0.019597012549638748, -0.01821731962263584, -0.007233347278088331, -0.020199792459607124, 0.0008007750730030239, -0.002858176827430725, -0.0154043510556221, -0.006834843195974827, 0.001168721355497837, 0.00684154080